Aura is a media and broadcast-content aid. What its host says - including
song summaries and scripts written by a language model, and transcripts made
by speech recognition - is not verified fact. Model-written text should be read
by a person before it is relied on or broadcast, and anything urgent or
safety-related must go out through the deploying organisation's own checked
announcement process, never through generated content alone.

Aura does not transmit. Any broadcast of its audio is made by, and is the
responsibility of, whoever operates the transmitter, including its licensing
and frequency authorisation.
